The dictionaries are data; the grapheme-to-phoneme code that reads them is a Java port written for
this module (com.integrallis.models.audio.phonemizer). misaki's eSpeak NG fallback is not bundled.

Letter-to-phoneme fallback models beside them, g2p-us.onnx and g2p-gb.onnx with their symbol
tables g2p-us.json and g2p-gb.json, were trained for this module on those dictionaries and are
licensed with it under the Apache License 2.0. Recipe, held-out accuracy and agreement with the
publisher's eSpeak fallback: experiments/paradee-8m-tts/g2p/ in the Models repository. They stand
in for misaki's eSpeak NG fallback, which is GPL-3.0 and is not bundled.

cmudict-us.json beside them is derived from CMUdict (cmusphinx/cmudict, Copyright (C) 1993-2015
Carnegie Mellon University, BSD-2-Clause; license text: META-INF/licenses/cmudict.txt): the words
misaki's American dictionaries lack, with CMUdict's ARPAbet converted to misaki's spelling by
experiments/paradee-8m-tts/g2p/cmudict_to_misaki.py in the Models repository. The conversion is
measured against misaki's own entries where both have a word; the report is beside the script.

